49	/// A Peer dereferences to its opaque type:
50	/// This allows the router code to take ownership of the opaque type
51	/// used for callback events, while still enabling the rest of the code to access the opaque type
52	/// (which might expose other functionality in their scope) from a Peer pointer.
53	///
54	/// e.g. it can take ownership of the timer state of a peer.
55	impl<E: Endpoint, C: Callbacks, T: tun::Writer, B: udp::Writer<E>> Deref for PeerInner<E, C, T, B> {
